# Local dev secrets for `wrangler dev` (copy to .dev.vars, which is git-ignored).
# In production set these with: wrangler secret put <NAME>
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your-oauth-app-client-id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your-oauth-app-client-secret
COOKIE_SECRET=a-long-random-string
# The GitHub App (docs/architecture/github-app.md). GITHUB_CLIENT_ID / GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET above are the
# App's own client id and secret. The four below let an org connect its repositories by installing it;
# leave them out and Org settings offers only the pasted-token path.
# GITHUB_APP_SLUG=your-app-url-name
# GITHUB_APP_ID=123456
# GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=the-webhook-secret-set-on-the-app
# The .pem GitHub generated, on ONE line with \n for each line break:
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n…\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"
# Key-encryption key for per-org integration secrets (Org settings › Integrations): 32 random bytes, base64.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32   — unset, the Integrations API answers 503 secrets_unavailable.
TROV_KEK=replace-with-openssl-rand-base64-32

# ── Local stand-ins for the services Trov calls ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two values, one rule (src/platform/loopback.ts): each is honoured ONLY when it is plain http on
# 127.0.0.1 or localhost — https, any other host and anything unparseable are ignored — and NEVER while
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is a live key (sk_live_… / rk_live_…). Never set either as a deployed secret: a
# deployed Worker ignores them (and could not reach loopback if it did not).
#
# LOCAL_UPSTREAM — GitHub and Gemini, during a Sync GitHub and its closing refresh
# (src/sync/local-upstream.ts, docs/architecture/sync.md › Trying it locally). Requests to
# api.github.com go to <base>/github/… and to generativelanguage.googleapis.com to <base>/gemini/….
# The webhook, the cron and sign-in are not rerouted.
# LOCAL_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8862
#
# STRIPE_TEST_API_BASE — Stripe's API, for every billing call (src/billing/config.ts,
# docs/architecture/billing.md › Configuration). Needs the two Stripe secrets set to TEST values.
# STRIPE_TEST_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8842
# (Embedded checkout — STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, a `pk_test_…` key — is never on beside this stand-in: it
#  has no Stripe.js to serve, so a local checkout is always the stand-in's plain hosted page. To see the
#  embedded form locally, use real Stripe TEST keys with no STRIPE_TEST_API_BASE. docs/architecture/billing.md.)
# To walk the paid flows with no Stripe account: run `node scripts/dev/stripe-standin.mjs` (it listens on
# that port, serves a stand-in checkout and portal, and delivers signed webhooks) and set
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_local_standin and STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_local_standin beside it.
#
# Summaries are off without a key (docs/architecture/plans.md › AI summaries). With LOCAL_UPSTREAM set,
# any non-empty value turns them on against the stand-in.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-key
